From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 19:32:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Bravery: tap to scroll, banner hiding and toolbar
 auto-hide

Tap to scroll: BraveContentView reports page touches to BraveryController.
A tap that the renderer reports as unhandled, inside a scroll zone, becomes
a short synthetic drag at the tap point, so it scrolls the scroller under
the finger and hides the toolbar like a real swipe. A Blink plaster makes
taps the page reacted to (DOM/style change, focusable element or ARIA
widget) count as handled.

Banner hiding: "Auto-hide banner" / "Remove banner" in the long-press menu
(including empty areas, where Chromium sends a page menu with no items) and
"Hide banner" in the text selection menu. A script in Brave's internal
isolated world finds the outermost fixed/sticky element, hides it, and the
rule is remembered per site (not in private tabs).

Toolbar: upstream pins the URL bar whenever an accessibility service that
can perform gestures runs (e.g. Tap2Scroll). A plaster makes that a setting.

Settings > Bravery holds all of it.
